# November 19, 2026: Carbon County, Wyoming (region wy), drawn at random by tools/choose.py. The Atlas had one place in
# Wyoming (the Piedmont kilns). This batch takes the county's railroad and copper-boom towns along the Union Pacific and
# the old Lincoln Highway: an Army post of 1868 that guarded the railroad crossing of the North Platte, the 1901 state
# penitentiary, two depots, a coal-camp ghost town, the Grand Encampment copper district's museum and opera house, a
# 1920s oil company town, three old hotels still taking guests, the dinosaur-bone Fossil Cabin (moved in May 2026), and
# an airway beacon field of 1929. Sources were opened in this session: Wikipedia as raw text (tools/wiki_raw.py); the
# National Register forms for the Boston-Wyoming smelter and Ferris-Haggarty mine (1973), Parco (1987), Carbon Cemetery
# (2010) and the Medicine Bow intermediate field (2012) from NPGallery (text layer read); and through tools/page.py the
# managers' and owners' pages (Wyoming State Parks, the Wyoming Frontier Prison, the City of Rawlins, the Carbon County
# Visitors Council, the hotels' own sites), WyoHistory.org, WyoFile, HMdb and Cowboy State Daily.
from data_b import N
from data_ma import W
def L(t,u): return [t,u]
BATCH={'key':'wy_iwfl','label':'Carbon County, Wyoming','added':'2026-11-19 03:56'}
